            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nGastronomic. Fresh from Japan. Clever use of ingredients. Great chef.\nJun 2022\nWe had Akane and Musho Omakase served to us by our jovial Malaysian chef with 30 years of experience in Shanghai, Thailand, and Singapore, which we connected over.\n\nWhat we loved:\n- Truly fresh catches and great quality in all their ingredients, air-flown weekly from Japan. You can taste the sweetness in the melons, the wagyu, and definitely the fishes since they were so fresh. Even their various seaweeds were juicy and their wasabi (jelly?) was freshly made.\n\n- Clever use of fusion ingredients such as truffle and caviar in various dishes. We were also spoilt with their generous use of uni (urchins), good-sized abalone, and gold flakes to impress.\n\n- Chef was clearly swift and experienced in his knife work - a joy to watch. Presentation of dishes was exquisite.\n\n- Just 50 metres from Ben Thanh Market, the very hidden entrance (a simple door literally on the side of a normal clothing store of a two-storey building) and the secretive dark entryway to this soothingly-dimmed restaurant, somehow made the entire experience rather exclusive yet exciting. The bar upstairs, together with the centrality of this location, seemed like a cool place to hold private events for probably up to 15 people (per floor).\n\nExpensive. But worth it.\nRead more\nWritten July 6, 2022",
