            "review_text": "hoanghac13\nSan Jose, California641 contributions\n0\nThe best Omakase in HCM city\nMay 2022 • Friends\nSo far the best Omakase meal in Vietnam. A must try while in HCM city.\n\nI chose the 3.6mil+ set with 16 dishes for me and my cousin. Food was fresh and delicious. I believe chef Sean said Friday and Tuesday are the day they get shipment. And all their fish are from Japan, not Indonesia, Malaysia or VietNam. Thumbs up 👍 \n\nI like Hamachi and Otoro but unfortunately those wasn’t offered in the meal. Chu Toro was, and it was as good as Otoro without the “necessary fat” 😂😂\n\nMain course I had the cold noodle made with angel hair, sadly not with my prefer Soba noodle. But the chef explain that Soba noodle is too thick for this dish. My cousin chose the beef with foie gras over rice and he said it was heavenly melted in his mouth.\n\nAll in all food was excellent, not too much nor too little. Services was attentive. \n\nI noticed plum wine or any wine is extremely expensive in Vietnam. They marked up x8-10 at least. I paid $9.94 for a bottle of Choya plum wine at Costco but here it was 1.8mil~$70-75. This is fine with me because I like to sip on plum wine while dining on sushi and sashimi. Thus, this is just a head up and don’t be surprised.\n\nI am planning to go back for another meal as I write this review. My mouth is actually watering as I reminiscing on the food. Again highly recommend, go try if you’re around. \n\nP/S: it situated in a small alley without any sign so call when you get there and the staff will escort you in. Enjoy!\nRead more\nWritten May 18, 2022",
